      "old_text": "Part (1) proves itself. If $J \\subset R_n$ is a two-sided ideal, then\n$J = \\bigoplus e_{ii}Je_{jj}$ and all of the summands $e_{ii}Je_{jj}$ are\nequal to each other and are a two-sided ideal $I$ of $R$. This proves (2).",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "BRAUER-002",
      "replacement_bytes": 225,
      "replacement_sha256": "76879FD996862B05EF615095886C444707B5A66D4809212E49226D84F25A6462",
      "replacement_text": "Part (1) proves itself. If $J \\subset R_n$ is a two-sided ideal, then\n$J = \\bigoplus e_{ii}Je_{jj}$, and the sets of $(i,j)$-entries occurring\nin $e_{ii}Je_{jj}$ are all equal to a two-sided ideal $I$ of $R$.\nThis proves (2).",
      "source_end_line": 276,
      "source_start_line": 274,
      "stable_id": "MC-STK-ERR-0745",
      "start_byte": 9254
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1917,
